    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To satisfy the structural complexity requirements while maintaining clarity, I have expanded the procedures into more granular checkpoints.\n\n**Nexus-7 LIDAR Sensor: Field Deployment Guide**\n\n**System Specifications Review**\n*   **Model Designation:** Nexus-7 LIDAR\n*   **Electrical Input Range:** 12V–24V DC operation\n*   **Physical Connector Type:** Standard 4-pin M12 Interface\n\n**Installation and Connection Protocol**\n1.  **Mounting Phase:** Securely affix the sensor unit onto the target chassis structure.\n    *   Verify that the optical lens surface is completely clear of all surface debris or foreign matter before proceeding.\n2.  **Electrical Integration:** Connect the power leads strictly according to the pin mapping:\n    *   Power Input: Connect to Pins 1 and 2.\n    *   Ground Reference: Connect to Pin 3.\n    *   Signal Data: Connect to Pin 4.\n3.  **Calibration Sequence Initiation:** Once the unit indicates readiness (status LED displays solid green), access the terminal and run the designated command: `nexus_cal`.\n\n**Critical Safety Directives**\n*   **Visual Hazard:** Never directly observe",
      "source": "target",
